    {
      "id": "guarded-noop-phase-validation",
      "name": "Guarded No-op Phase Validation",
      "description": "Fix the guarded controller so inspection phases (clarify, analyze) can pass without modifying a file when the pre-existing artifact already satisfies deterministic, phase-specific validations, without weakening any existing false-success protection.",
      "source_requirements": [
        "NPV-001",
        "NPV-002",
        "NPV-003",
        "NPV-004",
        "NPV-005",
        "NPV-006",
        "NPV-007",
        "NPV-008",
        "NPV-009",
        "NPV-010",
        "NPV-011",
        "NPV-012"
      ],
      "acceptance_criteria": [
        "each phase is classified as produce-or-update, inspect-or-update, or execute",
        "clarify can pass without changing spec.md when the active spec is complete and unambiguous",
        "analyze can pass without changing files when there are no blocking findings",
        "a structured phase_result block is required to promote any no-op",
        "the active artifact is resolved via .specify/feature.json, never an ambiguous glob",
        "producer phases still require a change on their first valid run",
        "missing_artifact, unchanged_artifact, and valid_noop are distinguished",
        "user_decision_required pauses the workflow immediately without consuming an attempt",
        "allowlists, path protection, and simulated-tool-call detection remain intact",
        "a previously-blocked attempt can be recoverably revalidated under a new contract version",
        "policy, contract version, outcome, and artifact hashes are recorded in attempt state",
        "already-completed workflows remain compatible (no destructive state migration)",
        "the existing 95-test suite from feature 1 continues to pass",
        "the qwen-greeting-api case can leave the clarify block without artificially editing the spec",
        "the final report distinguishes artifact_updated from no_changes_required"
      ],
      "dependencies": [
        "guarded-mode-controller"
      ],
